    "depth": "0 = no reference to another unit; otherwise 1 + max depth of the referenced units. Edges: mapping_spec decision.references, plus the two edge kinds the spec cannot carry \u2014 history_copy of_table (F52) and the unenforced CUST_ID chain INVOICE_HEADER->CUSTOMER_MASTER (F48). Dangling TENANT_ID columns (customerMaster, invoiceHeader, hist tables; 0-1 of N resolve) are raw strings and add no edge.",
    "estimate": "documents = fixture_counts tables_total of the root table; bytes = rows x data_profile row_bytes avg per contributing table (root, embedded children minus orphans, extended-reference parent row as upper bound); max_doc_bytes_upper_bound = max root row + max embedded bytes per parent (handcheck) or max child row x max fan-out. Oracle VSIZE bytes, so BSON documents will be somewhat larger (field names, type tags).",
    "wave": "d-waves: one wave. The reference layer (codes, tenants, plans; reference_layer: true) is depth 0 but nothing downstream needs it in the target before it can be reconciled: every reference is kept as the raw source key and every extended reference (invoices.tenant, subscriptions.plan) is copied from the source parent row at load time, and recon compares each collection against its own source tables. Depth therefore orders batches, it does not gate waves."
  },
